---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';
---

<Base title="about" description="About sabfodel, physics student." wide>
  <header class="entry-head">
    <span class="kicker">about</span>
    <h1>About me</h1>
  </header>

  <div class="ab">
    <figure class="ab__photo">
      <img src="/img/me/me-square.jpg" alt="sabfodel on a balcony" width="480" height="480" loading="eager" />
    </figure>

    <div class="prose ab__text">
      {/* TODO: gerçek adını eklemek istersen buraya yaz. */}
      <p class="lede">
        I'm a third-year physics student in Turkey. I go by sabfodel online.
      </p>
      <p>
        I like to understand things by writing them as code. That's how I ended up with a black
        hole ray tracer, an N-body solar system and a quantum circuit simulator, all in Rust and
        without physics libraries. I check the results against things I know are true:
        conservation laws, analytical solutions and known numbers.
      </p>
      <p>
        I want to work on quantum computing. I'm also reading about physics in medicine and
        biology, but that part is still new to me.
      </p>

      <h2>Education</h2>
      {/* TODO: üniversite adını ve beklenen mezuniyet yılını ekle. */}
      <table>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">BSc Physics</th><td>3rd year</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Qiskit Global Summer School</th><td>completed</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">QWorld QBronze</th><td>in progress</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>Tools</h2>
      <table>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Languages</th><td>Rust, Python</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Quantum</th><td>Qiskit, my own state-vector simulator</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Numerics</th><td>RK4, Monte Carlo sampling, Rayon</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Data</th><td>NumPy, pandas, scikit-learn, Matplotlib</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Writing</th><td>LaTeX, Markdown, Emacs org-mode</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Email me at <a data-mail-u={SITE.mailUser} data-mail-d={SITE.mailDomain} data-mail-show href="#contact">{SITE.mailUser} [at] {SITE.mailDomain}</a>.
        My code is on <a href={SITE.github}>GitHub</a>.
        {SITE.linkedin && <> I'm also on <a href={SITE.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a>.</>}
        {SITE.cv && <> My <a href={SITE.cv}>CV</a> is here.</>}
      </p>

    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .ab {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 320px minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(1.6rem, 4vw, 3.6rem);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .ab__photo { margin: 0; }

  .ab__photo img {
    display: block;
    width: 320px;
    height: 320px;
    object-fit: cover;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-2);
  }

  .ab__text { max-width: 62ch; }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .ab { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
    .ab__photo img { width: 220px; height: 220px; }
  }
</style>
